WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:09.243
Early Saturday morning Ben floated through the kitchen.

2
00:00:09.244 --> 00:00:12.515
He was heading for the door when Uncle Bert stopped him.

3
00:00:12.516 --> 00:00:17.251
"You're just in time, Ben!" His uncle was floating near the stove, cooking.

4
00:00:17.252 --> 00:00:22.348
"I'm making my famous mudberry paincakes."

5
00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:26.459
"Paincakes?" Ben's stomach rumbled.

6
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.627
"I was going to skip breakfast today, but I can't resist your paincakes."

7
00:00:31.628 --> 00:00:36.310
"Neither can anyone else." Uncle Bert laughed.

8
00:00:36.311 --> 00:00:43.634
"That's why I named my restaurant Bert's House of Paincakes."

9
00:00:43.635 --> 00:00:46.814
Ben sat down to eat.

10
00:00:46.815 --> 00:00:49.919
"Do you miss the restaurant since you sold it?"

11
00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:57.561
"Sometimes. But now I have time to travel, and I can take care of you and Sid when your parents go out of town.

12
00:00:57.562 --> 00:01:00.956
Eat up!" Uncle Bert smiled.

13
00:01:00.957 --> 00:01:08.779
"I tell you, Ben, you're a lucky ghost. Macdeath is my favorite Quakespeare play.

14
00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:12.283
And that's exciting about the professional actress who's directing the play.

15
00:01:12.284 --> 00:01:14.641
What's her name?"

16
00:01:14.642 --> 00:01:21.591
"Uncle Bert!" Sid yelled from upstairs. "Do I smell paincakes?"

17
00:01:21.592 --> 00:01:27.526
"You sure do," Uncle Bert called back. "Come get some, Sid!"

18
00:01:27.527 --> 00:01:30.704
Ben suddenly had a question for Uncle Bert too.

19
00:01:30.705 --> 00:01:35.262
"Hey, Uncle Bert. Do you know anything about the curse of Macdeath

20
00:01:35.263 --> 00:01:37.970
? Everybody keeps talking about

21
00:01:37.971 --> 00:01:43.700
it." "Curse?" Uncle Bert laughed. "There's no such

22
00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:45.393
thing." "Are you sure?"

23
00:01:45.394 --> 00:01:49.350
"Absolutely! That's pure superstition. I—"

24
00:01:49.351 --> 00:01:54.965
Uncle Bert knocked over the salt shaker with his flipper, sending salt flying.

25
00:01:54.966 --> 00:02:00.800
"Oops!" He quickly took a pinch of the spilled salt and threw it over his left shoulder.

26
00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:03.432
"Why'd you do that?" Ben asked.

27
00:02:03.433 --> 00:02:08.769
"Spilling salt is bad luck. This undoes it," Uncle Bert said.

28
00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:12.652
"But isn't that a superstition?" Ben asked.

29
00:02:12.653 --> 00:02:17.050
"Hmm . . ." Uncle Bert shrugged. "I guess so."

30
00:02:17.051 --> 00:02:21.914
The conversation was making Ben feel more worried about the school play.

31
00:02:21.915 --> 00:02:26.388
So he finished his stack of paincakes and picked up his script again.

32
00:02:26.389 --> 00:02:34.162
"Thanks for breakfast, Uncle Bert. I'll see you later—I have rehearsal all day today."

33
